      "writtenOn": "2017-08-14T22:40:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With further investigation, it seems the XT_QTAGUID_UID have no effect on the code here, since when the program reaches this section, XT_QTAGUID_GID must be true, so (XT_QTAGUID_UID | XT_QTAGUID_GID) will always be true no matter how XT_QTAGUID_UID changes. And if there is a inverted gid match, the packet from a closed socket should be dropped since the gid of that packet is null and only packet with a specific gid could pass for a inverted rule.",
      "parentUuid": "076fa0f4_5ceca5ca",
      "range": {
